Z||000000||JohnAC||06-23-2001||03:42 AM||||I just got my 88' SE two weeks ago.  It has a nice crack in the front end and a small crack in the driver side fender (I feel sorry for the car, whoever drove it before me was a moron!)  When I got it had a bad wheel bearing (wheel literally sat at an angle) and needed a valve cover gasket and some other odds and ends.  I didn't fix the front-end yet because I'm not sure what I want to do with it.  I'm thinking about customizing the car and stickin a 3.8 in it, replacin da 3-speed auto w/ a 5speed manual and changing the body panels to GT.  Eventually I also wanted it painted blue w/ blue headlamps/blinkers and puttin in sequential taillights.  Basically I am not sure what I want to do with it, maybe I'll just rebuild the engine and leave it w/ the 4cyl (just add some high performance options to it!)  Any recommendations??  Basically I'm wondering what engine/what body style/internal options etc.<P>Also, I was wondering about an AWD tranny.  That is just an afterthought though.<p>[This message has been edited by JohnAC (edited 06-23-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||06-23-2001||09:03 AM||||If you have lots of money, time or skill, you can do anything to your Fiero.<P>You can easily drop $10K into engine upgrade, transmission swaps, upgrade suspension, brakes and body repair and paint. Remember you get what you pay for.<P>Most any body panel will fit on any Fiero.  It may look like a GT but VIN# says SE.||||reg||1
